# Loaded only by `vite build --mode android-qa` (web/package.json's
# build:android-qa script) — a QA-only Android build variant used
# EXCLUSIVELY during offline-first time-tracking development/testing.
# `.env.android` (the real production Android build, used for the APK real
# employees install) is never read or modified by this file, and this file
# is never read by `build:android` — the two modes are fully independent.
#
# Points at the developer machine's own LAN address so a real Android phone
# on the same Wi-Fi can reach the LOCAL dev API server (server/src/index.ts,
# port 4000) directly — never the production Railway deployment. This
# matters for two reasons: (1) the offline-sync endpoints this QA build
# exercises don't exist on the deployed production server at all until this
# work is explicitly pushed, and (2) it keeps every destructive/offline-
# replay/conflict/clock-change test scenario off the real production
# database's real employee records, confined to disposable QA-tagged
# fixtures on the local dev server instead.
#
# Re-run `ipconfig`/`ifconfig` and update this if the dev machine's LAN IP
# changes (e.g. a different Wi-Fi network) — it is not auto-detected.
VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.3.63:4000
